@testray.main.component.name = "Support QA"
@type = "koroneiki"

Feature: Koroneiki Team and Contact API
	Testing Koroneiki Team API functionality in relation to Contacts.

Teardown:
	* I tear down the contacts on koroneiki with the following email addresses
	| koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| koroneiki.contact2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	* I tear down the teams on koroneiki with the following names
	| Development Team |
	| Marketing Team   |
	| Engineering Team |
	| Sales Team       |
	* I tear down the accounts on koroneiki with the following names
	| Koroneiki Auto Subsidiary |
	| Koroneiki Engr Subsidiary |
	| Koroneiki Automotive      |
	| Koroneiki Engineering     |

Scenario: Assign contact to team
	Koroneiki contacts should be able to be assigned to teams.

	Given I create a contact on koroneiki with the following values
	| Email Address | koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | Koroneiki                                |
	| Language      | English                                  |
	| Last Name     | Contact1                                 |
	| Middle Name   | User                                     |
	| Okta ID       | koroneikicontact1                        |
	And I create an account on koroneiki with the following values
	| Code         | KORAUTO                                  |
	| Description  | Test automotive account on koroneiki     |
	| Fax Number   | 555-555-1234                             |
	| Industry     | Automotive                               |
	| Name         | Koroneiki Automotive                     |
	| Notes        | Additional account notes                 |
	| Phone Number | 555-555-5678                             |
	| Sold By      | Liferay US                               |
	| Status       | Approved                                 |
	| Tier         | Regular                                  |
	| Website      | www.koroneikiautomotive.com              |
	And I create a team with the name "Development Team" for the account "Koroneiki Automotive"
	And I assign contacts with the following email addresses to the team "Development Team"
	| koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	Then the contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should be assigned the team "Development Team"

Scenario: Assign contact to team via okta id
	Koroneiki contacts should be able to be assigned to accounts via okta id.

	Given I create a contact on koroneiki with the following values
	| Email Address | koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | Koroneiki                                |
	| Language      | English                                  |
	| Last Name     | Contact1                                 |
	| Middle Name   | User                                     |
	| Okta ID       | koroneikicontact1                        |
	And I create an account on koroneiki with the following values
	| Code         | KORAUTO                                  |
	| Description  | Test automotive account on koroneiki     |
	| Fax Number   | 555-555-1234                             |
	| Industry     | Automotive                               |
	| Name         | Koroneiki Automotive                     |
	| Notes        | Additional account notes                 |
	| Phone Number | 555-555-5678                             |
	| Sold By      | Liferay US                               |
	| Status       | Approved                                 |
	| Tier         | Regular                                  |
	| Website      | www.koroneikiautomotive.com              |
	And I create a team with the name "Development Team" for the account "Koroneiki Automotive"
	And I assign contacts with the following okta IDs to the team "Development Team"
	| koroneikicontact1 |
	Then the contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should be assigned the team "Development Team"

Scenario: Assign separate contacts to separate teams
	Separate koroneiki contacts should be able to be assigned to separate teams.

	Given I create a contact on koroneiki with the following values
	| Email Address | koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | Koroneiki                                |
	| Language      | English                                  |
	| Last Name     | Contact1                                 |
	| Middle Name   | User                                     |
	| Okta ID       | koroneikicontact1                        |
	And I create a contact on koroneiki with the following values
	| Email Address | koroneiki.contact2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | Koroneiki                                |
	| Language      | English                                  |
	| Last Name     | Contact2                                 |
	| Middle Name   | User                                     |
	| Okta ID       | koroneikicontact2                        |
	And I create an account on koroneiki with the following values
	| Code         | KORAUTO                              |
	| Description  | Test automotive account on koroneiki |
	| Fax Number   | 555-555-1234                         |
	| Industry     | Automotive                           |
	| Name         | Koroneiki Automotive                 |
	| Notes        | Additional account notes             |
	| Phone Number | 555-555-5678                         |
	| Sold By      | Liferay US                           |
	| Status       | Approved                             |
	| Tier         | Regular                              |
	| Website      | www.koroneikiautomotive.com          |
	And I create a team with the name "Development Team" for the account "Koroneiki Automotive"
	And I create a team with the name "Marketing Team" for the account "Koroneiki Automotive"
	And I assign contacts with the following email addresses to the team "Development Team"
	| koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	And I assign contacts with the following email addresses to the team "Marketing Team"
	| koroneiki.contact2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	Then the contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should be assigned the team "Development Team"
	And the contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact2@lrcustomer.com.broken" should be assigned the team "Marketing Team"
	And the contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should not be assigned the team "Marketing Team"
	And the contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact2@lrcustomer.com.broken" should not be assigned the team "Development Team"

Scenario: Assign separate contacts to separate teams on separate accounts
	Separate koroneiki contacts should be able to be assigned to separate teams on separate accounts.

	Given I create a contact on koroneiki with the following values
